---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Facts from "../components/Facts.astro";

const keywords = ["Tangible", "Embodied", "Distributed", "Networked", "Sound", "Interaction"];
---
<Base>
  <h1 class="thesis">The Sound of Smart Things<span>Making the Invisible Audible</span></h1>

  <h2 class="label">Abstract</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Networked smart things are part of everyday environments, yet what they do, and how they relate, mostly goes unnoticed. Sound does not need to be seen to be heard: it can stay in the background or move into focus. TSOST investigates sound as an interaction material for distributed systems of smart things, by designing and building autonomous, sensing, networked, sound-producing devices. Its central artefact is TESI, a modular toolkit for tangible and embodied sound interaction.</p>
  </div>

  <ul class="keywords" aria-label="Keywords">
    <li class="label">Keywords</li>
    {keywords.map((k) => <li class="label">{k}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2 class="label">Project</h2>
  <Facts rows={[
    ["PhD Candidate", "Francesco Di Maggio"],
    ["Department", "Industrial Design, Eindhoven University of Technology"],
    ["Supervisors", "Bart Hengeveld, Berry Eggen"],
    ["Co-supervisor", "Rebecca Fiebrink, University of the Arts London"],
  ]} />

</Base>
